course: dictionary
lesson: 7560
title: Prepare: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word prepare has three main meanings. The sentence around it tells you which one is in use. Ask yourself what is being made ready, or who is getting ready, and for what.
explain: «Zoo kitchens prepare hundreds of meals a day.» Meals are food, so prepare means make food ready to eat. Swap in "get ready" and the sentence stops making sense.
explain: «The pharmacist prepares it and checks it is right.» Here prepare means make something ready to use. The pharmacist makes the medicine ready, then checks it.
explain: The word prepared also shows up in phrases. «Be prepared» means be ready for whatever happens, and «prepared to» means willing to do something. Read the words after prepare to find which one you have.
fact: Prepare means to make something ready to use, to get yourself ready for something that will happen, or to make food ready to eat.
fact: «Be prepared» is the motto of the Scouts, and it means ready for whatever happens.
fact: «Prepared to» means willing to do something, as in «prepared to help».
fact: You often prepare for a test or a trip, which means getting yourself ready for it.
fact: The forms are prepare, prepares, prepared and preparing, so check the ending to see when it happened.
exercise: «Behind every zoo is a busy kitchen where keepers prepare hundreds of meals a day.» What does prepare mean here? | Hide away | Make a loud noise | Get yourself ready for a trip | *Make food ready to eat
exercise: Ana must prepare for her spelling test on Friday. What does prepare mean here? | Pass the test without trying | *Get herself ready for it | Put the test in a bag | Cancel the test
exercise: «The pharmacist prepares it and checks it is right.» What does the pharmacist do with the medicine? | Throws it away | Eats it | *Makes it ready to use | Sells it to the doctor
test: «The altar or communion table is where the bread and wine are prepared for communion.» What does prepared mean here? | *Made ready | Put on a high shelf | Broken into small pieces | Thrown away
test: Which phrase means willing to do something? | Prepared dinner | Prepared the table | *Prepared to help | Prepared for a storm
exam: Which word in «Zoo kitchens prepare hundreds of meals a day» is the clue that prepare means make food? | Zoo | Hundreds | *Meals | Kitchens
